You may not distribute the software, or any changes or new works based on
it, only as a compiled binary, an installer, a hosted service, or any other
form that withholds the source code from the people who receive it.

## Additional Condition 2 — Your Responsibility

The software connects to cryptocurrency exchanges and can place orders,
convert assets, and withdraw funds automatically, including without a human
present. Those actions move real money and are generally irreversible.

  (a) You are solely responsible for how you configure, run, modify, and
      distribute the software, and for every trade, conversion, transfer,
      withdrawal, loss, tax consequence, missed execution, and exchange
      account action that results, whether or not it was what you intended.

  (b) Nothing in the software is financial, investment, tax, or legal
      advice. The licensor does not operate an exchange, hold your funds,
      hold your keys, or act as your broker, adviser, or custodian.

  (c) The software may contain defects, may stop running without warning,
      and may fail to execute an automation you configured. It is your
      responsibility to verify that it is doing what you expect.

  (d) You will not hold the licensor responsible for anything you or anyone
      you distribute to does with the software. To the extent the law
      allows, you will indemnify and hold the licensor harmless from any
      claim, loss, liability, or expense (including reasonable legal fees)
      brought by a third party and arising out of your use, modification, or
      distribution of the software.

  (e) You are responsible for complying with the laws, regulations, and
      exchange terms of service that apply where you are.

